<%- include("../../partials/portal-shell-head", {
  pageTitle: "Settings",
  pageLead: "Your photo, password and invoice address.",
  nav: "settings", student: student, avatarUrl: avatarUrl,
  initials: initials, hue: hue, notice: notice, error: error,
}) %>

<%- include('../../partials/billing-address') %>

<div class="sp-cols">
  <section>
    <%#
      The photo is resized to 256x256 in the browser before it is sent,
      and posted as a data: URL through the ordinary form encoding —
      so a 4MB phone photo leaves as about 20KB and the server needs
      no upload library. Without JavaScript the file input is hidden
      and the section says so, rather than offering a control that
      would silently do nothing.
    %>
    <div class="sp-card">
      <h2>Profile photo</h2>

      <div class="sp-photo">
        <%- include("../../partials/portal-avatar", {
          avatarUrl: avatarUrl, initials: initials, hue: hue,
          size: "lg", name: student.name,
        }) %>

        <div class="sp-photo-side">
          <p class="muted" style="font-size:.86rem;margin-top:0">
            A square picture works best. It is resized on your own device before
            it is sent, and only you and the office ever see it.
          </p>

          <form method="post" action="/portal/settings/avatar" data-avatar-form hidden>
            <input type="hidden" name="image" data-avatar-payload>
            <label class="btn btn-sm" style="cursor:pointer">
              <%= avatarUrl ? "Change photo" : "Upload a photo" %>
              <input type="file" accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp"
                     data-avatar-input hidden>
            </label>
            <span class="muted" style="margin-left:.6rem;font-size:.84rem" data-avatar-status></span>
          </form>

          <noscript>
            <p class="notice" style="margin:0">
              Uploading a photo needs JavaScript, because the picture is resized
              in your browser before it is sent. Everything else on this page
              works without it.
            </p>
          </noscript>

          <% if (avatarUrl) { %>
            <form method="post" action="/portal/settings/avatar" style="margin-top:.7rem"
                  data-confirm-delete="your profile photo">
              <input type="hidden" name="remove" value="1">
              <button class="linklike" type="submit">Remove my photo</button>
            </form>
          <% } %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sp-card">
      <h2>Password</h2>
      <form method="post" action="/portal/settings/password">
        <%- include("../../partials/password-field", {
          id: "current_password", name: "current_password", label: "Current password",
        }) %>
        <%- include("../../partials/password-field", {
          id: "new_password", name: "new_password", label: "New password",
          autocomplete: "new-password", minlength: 10,
          hint: "At least 10 characters, and not your own name or address.",
        }) %>
        <button class="btn" type="submit">Change my password</button>
      </form>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size:.82rem;margin:.9rem 0 0">
        Changing it signs out every other device. You stay signed in here.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside>
    <div class="sp-card">
      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <dl class="sp-facts">
        <div><dt>Email</dt><dd><%= student.email %></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Status</dt><dd><span class="pill pill-live"><%= student.status %></span></dd></div>
        <% if (student.last_login_at) { %>
          <div><dt>Last signed in</dt><dd>
            <%= new Date(student.last_login_at).toLocaleDateString("en-GB", { day: "numeric", month: "short", year: "numeric" }) %>
          </dd></div>
        <% } %>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="sp-card">
      <h2>Your data</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size:.86rem;margin-top:-.3rem">
        You can ask for a copy of everything we hold about you. That is your
        right under the GDPR and it costs nothing.
      </p>
      <p style="margin:0"><a href="/contact">Make a request</a> · <a href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a></p>
    </div>
  </aside>
</div>

<%#
  Deleting the account. Last on the page and in its own bordered card,
  because it is the one thing here that cannot be undone.

  The password is asked for even though they are signed in: a borrowed
  or unattended laptop should not be enough to erase somebody's
  account. On top of that the button opens the type-the-word dialog.

  What survives is stated plainly rather than buried in the privacy
  policy. Invoices have to be kept for ten years under German
  bookkeeping law and a certificate has to stay checkable for whoever
  it was shown to — a person deciding whether to delete deserves to
  know that before they do, not after.
%>
<div class="sp-card sp-danger" style="margin-top:1rem">
  <h2>Delete my account</h2>
  <p style="font-size:.9rem;margin-top:-.3rem">
    This closes your account and removes your photo, phone number, address,
    date of birth and password. You will be signed out everywhere and will not
    be able to sign in again.
  </p>
  <p class="muted" style="font-size:.86rem">
    Your invoices and any certificates already issued are kept — German
    bookkeeping law requires invoices to be held for ten years, and a
    certificate has to stay verifiable for whoever you showed it to. Those
    records keep the name they were issued under. Nothing else does.
  </p>

  <form method="post" action="/portal/settings/close" data-confirm-delete="your account">
    <label class="field" style="max-width:22rem">
      <span>Your password</span>
      <input type="password" name="password" required autocomplete="current-password">
    </label>
    <button class="btn btn-sm sp-danger-btn" type="submit">Delete my account</button>
  </form>
</div>

<%- include("../../partials/portal-shell-foot") %>
